## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the two or any byte of the product, a fixture or a golden; ANY minus line, or an existing line, helper, constant or assertion edited; a skip, removal, weakening or disabling; a planted or sent name that holds no refused character (the allowance never exercised); an edge character that is not an ASCII space, or a row pinning the B488-5 difference; any of the builder's five (A1, A2, A3 in either form, A4, A6) surviving every new row; a new row green at the base and red at the head's own product, or the class or the mock file red at the head and green at main alone; a lost or renamed test name, or an added name that is not one of the 12 new cases; the Api project or the web suite red at the head and green at main alone; a build warning or error; a merge conflict; overlap > 0 with a live lane that conflicts or shares a path; a request leaving loopback; a secret; the head moved. *Major:* a NEW mutant that WIDENS the allowance within property P (case, edge white space on either side, or length: N1-N9, A3b) surviving every new row; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (80/103, 107/63, the kill counts, 1901/13/0 and 1907/13/0, 2165 and 2171, 5/5, 0/0); T1 or T2 not turning R3 or (h) red (the rows would not read the stored text); a new row no mutant turns red; an instrument you cannot show faithful; a process, port or lock left; load discipline broken without figures. *Minor/Note (never a NO GO alone):* P1 (normalisation) or P2 surviving (outside the findings); the unmasked `UatOpenAssertionTests` drift if still present (a pre-existing defect, not this delta's); a comment that reads as an endorsement of the existing trim; a row's premise assertion without a second read; the order of the builder's survivor probe; B488-4, -5, -6 open; a 132-character held name that Azure SQL cannot hold. **Round 1 of 2: overall GO / GO WITH FINDINGS / NO GO; a NO GO sends a fix round to the builder: state the fix-shape in prose and the ONE-line question for the